    "g1": {"x": 0, "y": 4812, "w": 390, "fill": "green", "text": "G1 · Creators sign in with Apple (Google as fallback). Participants never need an account: anonymous session per device, and they can claim their results later by signing in."},
    "g2": {"x": 470, "y": 4812, "w": 390, "fill": "green", "text": "G2 · Any stop can be AI or hand-written. Add a stop by long-pressing the map or searching a place, then pick 'Suggest a question' or 'Write my own'. A fully manual quiz skips generation entirely."},
    "g3": {"x": 940, "y": 4812, "w": 390, "fill": "green", "text": "G3 · Three modes, creator decides which are allowed: Solo, Team on one phone (default), Team on several phones. With several phones the first answer counts for the team; teammates see it instantly."},
    "g4": {"x": 1410, "y": 4812, "w": 390, "fill": "green", "text": "G4 · Join any time before start; the walk unlocks at start time with a notification. Creator can open early from the monitor. After close: read-only results, no play."},
    "g5": {"x": 1880, "y": 4812, "w": 390, "fill": "green", "text": "G5 · Whole quiz downloads on join. Answers queue offline and sync later with timestamps. When GPS accuracy is worse than the stop radius, the radius widens automatically, up to 60 m."},
    "g6": {"x": 2350, "y": 4812, "w": 390, "fill": "green", "text": "G6 · 'I'm here' is accepted within 150 m (no speed bonus). Skip = 0 points, walk continues. 'Path blocked' alerts the creator, who can move or skip the stop live for everyone."}
